  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6309ec91-33d8-59a2-9220-0243dd51be4c" activityNameId="35503e9e-e7bf-5ad5-868e-82e9aae8ba82" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Printed wiring board, surface mount, lead-containing surface, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Printed wiring board, surface mount, lead-containing surface, at plant
The functional unit represents 1 m2 of a 6-layer FR-4 PWB, HAL (Sn-Pb) surface finished, with soldermask, for surface mount applications, without mounted components. It is designed to be used in ICT applications. Process data are taken from environmental reports of 3 German PWB producers, plus from literature. The described PWB has a square weight of 3.26 kg/m2.;
UUID: 59194bfe-9472-3333-89dc-9ab4d75490f8
The module covers the assembly of a PWB prepared for surface mounting of components. In this dataset (raw) materials, infrastructure, energy consumption, emissions to air and water and waste amounts from the production of 1 m2 of board are taken into account. Not included into this dataset is the mounting of the PWB.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Dataset comprises the following steps of PWB production: substrate preparation, imaging, exposure, etching, sandwiching, activation and accelaration steps as well as copper plating, cleaning, oxidification, dry vacuum lamination, micro etching, hot air levelling.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: $ 18.9315 Billion in 1998 (includes all rigid PWB)
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_59194bfe-9472-3333-89dc-9ab4d75490f8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
